{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:37:20+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "23e669e0b53401a8f771dedf4e1a0b21", "span_id": "53fcca174ef96d5f", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "4E8F5E0F", "msg": "{'role': 'tool', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call_response', 'id': 'fc_80122c99-8985-4d27-85cb-c8b509b4fda1', 'response': 'Based on First Abu Dhabi Bank (FAB) lending policies, the total cost of a banking loan is broken down into several components rather than being a single flat rate. \\n\\nHere is a simple explanation of how those components work:\\n\\n**1. Base Rate (Cost of Funds)**\\n*   **What it is:** This is the foundation of your interest rate. It represents the bank\\'s actual cost to obtain the money it is lending to you (e.g., raising deposits or borrowing from other banks).\\n*   **How it works:** This rate constantly changes based on the broader financial market. For example, in AED loans, it usually tracks a benchmark called **EIBOR**, and for USD loans, it tracks **SOFR**. \\n*   *(Source: FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual [Section 3.1]; FAB Credit Pricing Policy [Section 4])*\\n\\n**2. Credit Spread (Risk Margin)**\\n*   **What it is:** This is a percentage added on top of the Base Rate to cover the risk the bank is taking by lending to your specific company.\\n*   **How it works:** The bank looks at your credit rating (your financial health) and the duration of the loan. If your company is financially strong and low-risk, the spread will be small. If your company is riskier, the bank adds a higher spread to compensate for the chance of default. This is essentially the \"price\" of your creditworthiness.\\n*   *(Source: FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual [Section 3.1])*\\n\\n**3. Arrangement Fee**\\n*   **What it is:** A one-time, upfront fee.\\n*   **How it works:** This is charged when you sign the loan agreement or withdraw the first payment. It covers the bank\\'s initial administrative work, analysis, and processing required to set up the loan facility.\\n*   *(Source: FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual [Section 3.1])*\\n\\n**4. Commitment Fee**\\n*   **What it is:** A periodic fee charged on the portion of your loan that you **haven\\'t** used yet.\\n*   **How it works:** Banks often approve a credit limit (a facility) and let you take out money whenever you need it up to that limit. Even if you only use a little bit, the bank charges a small percentage on the unused, remaining balance. This is a fee for \"keeping the money available\" for you.\\n*   *(Source: FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual [Section 3.1])*\\n\\n**5. Agency Fee (For Large/Complex Loans only)**\\n*   **What it is:** An administrative fee for managing loans involving multiple banks.\\n*   **How it works:** For very large loans, one bank cannot lend all the money alone, so a group of banks shares the loan. If FAB acts as the manager (\"Facility Agent\") for the group,'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:37:21+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "23e669e0b53401a8f771dedf4e1a0b21", "span_id": "53fcca174ef96d5f", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "4E8F5E0F", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'text', 'content': '**Interest breakup – simple explanation**\\n\\n| Component | What it means | How it works (simple) |\\n|-----------|---------------|-----------------------|\\n| **Base Rate (Cost of Funds)** | The starting point of the loan’s interest. | It reflects the bank’s own cost of getting the money it lends you. In AED loans it follows **EIBOR**, in USD loans it follows **SOFR**. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1; FAB Credit Pricing Policy – Section\\u202f4)* |\\n| **Credit Spread (Risk Margin)** | Extra percentage added for the risk the bank takes. | The bank looks at your credit rating and loan term. Better rating\\u202f=\\u202fsmaller spread; higher risk\\u202f=\\u202flarger spread. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1)* |\\n| **Arrangement Fee** | One‑time upfront charge. | Paid when the loan agreement is signed or the first draw is made. It covers the bank’s paperwork and analysis to set up the facility. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1)* |\\n| **Commitment Fee** | Ongoing charge on the unused part of the approved limit. | Even if you haven’t drawn the full amount, the bank charges a small % on the remaining credit to keep it available for you. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1)* |\\n| **Agency Fee (large/complex loans only)** | Fee for managing a syndicated loan. | When many banks share a big loan and FAB acts as the manager, it gets this administrative fee. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1)* |\\n\\n**How to read it** – The total cost you pay = **Base Rate + Credit Spread** (this forms the “interest rate” you see) plus the **Arrangement Fee** (once) and the **Commitment Fee** (periodically) and, if applicable, an **Agency Fee**. Each piece has its own purpose, making the overall pricing transparent.'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:37:21+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "23e669e0b53401a8f771dedf4e1a0b21", "span_id": "2a63f2a330ddf4fa", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "4E8F5E0F", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call', 'id': 'fc_80122c99-8985-4d27-85cb-c8b509b4fda1', 'name': 'query_knowledge_base', 'arguments': '{\"question\":\"Explain the interest breakup components in simple terms for a banking loan\"}'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:37:21+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "23e669e0b53401a8f771dedf4e1a0b21", "span_id": "2a63f2a330ddf4fa", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "4E8F5E0F", "msg": "{'role': 'tool', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call_response', 'id': 'fc_80122c99-8985-4d27-85cb-c8b509b4fda1', 'response': 'Based on First Abu Dhabi Bank (FAB) lending policies, the total cost of a banking loan is broken down into several components rather than being a single flat rate. \\n\\nHere is a simple explanation of how those components work:\\n\\n**1. Base Rate (Cost of Funds)**\\n*   **What it is:** This is the foundation of your interest rate. It represents the bank\\'s actual cost to obtain the money it is lending to you (e.g., raising deposits or borrowing from other banks).\\n*   **How it works:** This rate constantly changes based on the broader financial market. For example, in AED loans, it usually tracks a benchmark called **EIBOR**, and for USD loans, it tracks **SOFR**. \\n*   *(Source: FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual [Section 3.1]; FAB Credit Pricing Policy [Section 4])*\\n\\n**2. Credit Spread (Risk Margin)**\\n*   **What it is:** This is a percentage added on top of the Base Rate to cover the risk the bank is taking by lending to your specific company.\\n*   **How it works:** The bank looks at your credit rating (your financial health) and the duration of the loan. If your company is financially strong and low-risk, the spread will be small. If your company is riskier, the bank adds a higher spread to compensate for the chance of default. This is essentially the \"price\" of your creditworthiness.\\n*   *(Source: FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual [Section 3.1])*\\n\\n**3. Arrangement Fee**\\n*   **What it is:** A one-time, upfront fee.\\n*   **How it works:** This is charged when you sign the loan agreement or withdraw the first payment. It covers the bank\\'s initial administrative work, analysis, and processing required to set up the loan facility.\\n*   *(Source: FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual [Section 3.1])*\\n\\n**4. Commitment Fee**\\n*   **What it is:** A periodic fee charged on the portion of your loan that you **haven\\'t** used yet.\\n*   **How it works:** Banks often approve a credit limit (a facility) and let you take out money whenever you need it up to that limit. Even if you only use a little bit, the bank charges a small percentage on the unused, remaining balance. This is a fee for \"keeping the money available\" for you.\\n*   *(Source: FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual [Section 3.1])*\\n\\n**5. Agency Fee (For Large/Complex Loans only)**\\n*   **What it is:** An administrative fee for managing loans involving multiple banks.\\n*   **How it works:** For very large loans, one bank cannot lend all the money alone, so a group of banks shares the loan. If FAB acts as the manager (\"Facility Agent\") for the group,'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:37:21+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "23e669e0b53401a8f771dedf4e1a0b21", "span_id": "2a63f2a330ddf4fa", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "4E8F5E0F", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'text', 'content': '**Interest breakup – simple explanation**\\n\\n| Component | What it means | How it works (simple) |\\n|-----------|---------------|-----------------------|\\n| **Base Rate (Cost of Funds)** | The starting point of the loan’s interest. | It reflects the bank’s own cost of getting the money it lends you. In AED loans it follows **EIBOR**, in USD loans it follows **SOFR**. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1; FAB Credit Pricing Policy – Section\\u202f4)* |\\n| **Credit Spread (Risk Margin)** | Extra percentage added for the risk the bank takes. | The bank looks at your credit rating and loan term. Better rating\\u202f=\\u202fsmaller spread; higher risk\\u202f=\\u202flarger spread. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1)* |\\n| **Arrangement Fee** | One‑time upfront charge. | Paid when the loan agreement is signed or the first draw is made. It covers the bank’s paperwork and analysis to set up the facility. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1)* |\\n| **Commitment Fee** | Ongoing charge on the unused part of the approved limit. | Even if you haven’t drawn the full amount, the bank charges a small % on the remaining credit to keep it available for you. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1)* |\\n| **Agency Fee (large/complex loans only)** | Fee for managing a syndicated loan. | When many banks share a big loan and FAB acts as the manager, it gets this administrative fee. *(FAB Corporate Term Loan Product Manual – Section\\u202f3.1)* |\\n\\n**How to read it** – The total cost you pay = **Base Rate + Credit Spread** (this forms the “interest rate” you see) plus the **Arrangement Fee** (once) and the **Commitment Fee** (periodically) and, if applicable, an **Agency Fee**. Each piece has its own purpose, making the overall pricing transparent.'}]}"}
