{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:49:31+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "9cb7492188c8bd799f9c57e49bb8875a", "span_id": "c1ef641da3f39790", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "7A3DF87F", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'text', 'content': \"Based on the **FAB Model Risk Management Framework (v3.1)** and the **CBUAE Circular No. 2024/BSE/047**, the following outlines FAB's comprehensive Model Risk Management (MRM) framework and specific validation requirements.\\n\\n### 1. Governance and Model Classification\\nThe MRM framework aligns with US Federal Reserve (SR 11-7) and CBUAE regulatory standards. The Framework is governed by the Chief Risk Officer and approved by the Board Risk & Compliance Committee.\\n*   **AI Risk Officer**: Senior management (CRO level or above) must be appointed to oversee regulatory compliance **[CBUAE 2024/BSE/047, Art. 2.1.2]**.\\n*   **Model Inventory**: A centralized, up-to-date inventory must be maintained for all AI/ML systems deployed in material business processes **[CBUAE 2024/BSE/047, Art. 2.2.1]**.\\n*   **Risk Classification**: Models are tiered based on materiality:\\n    *   **Tier 1 (High)**: Direct P&L impact or influence on credit decisions/pricing (e.g., IFRS 9 models, Credit Pricing AI agents). *Requirement: Full independent validation before deployment & annually thereafter.*\\n    *   **Tier 2 (Medium)**: Indirect impact (e.g., behavioral scoring). *Requirement: Targeted validation & biennial reviews.*\\n    *   **Tier 3 (Low)**: Minimal impact. *Requirement: Self-certification.*\\n    *(Source: FAB Model Risk Management Framework v3.1, Section 2)*.\\n\\n### 2. Documentation Requirements: The Model Evidence Pack (MEP)\\nFor every Tier 1 or Tier 2 model, a **Model Evidence Pack (MEP)** must be maintained as the primary audit document **[FAB MRM Framework, Sec. 3]**. Mandatory components include:\\n\\n**Core MEP Components:**\\n*   **Model Overview**: Name, ID, purpose, and deployment status.\\n*   **Design Documentation**: Theoretical basis, mathematical formulation, and assumptions.\\n*   **Data & Performance**: Training data sources, quality assessments, and in-sample/out-of-sample performance metrics.\\n*   **Validation Record**: Findings, weaknesses, and remediation actions.\\n*   **Limitations & F\"}]}"}
