{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:51:49+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "9cb7492188c8bd799f9c57e49bb8875a", "span_id": "8b66c3f7d16cc9e0", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "7A3DF87F", "msg": "{'role': 'tool', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call_response', 'id': 'fc_5cf2496d-e84a-4a28-bea6-29095b50ab24', 'response': 'Here is the complete pricing recommendation data for customer **CUST002**:\\n\\n| Field | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| **deal_id** | DEAL005 |\\n| **deal_date** | 2025-10-24 00:00:00 |\\n| **customer_id** | CUST002 |\\n| **customer_name** | Falcon Steel Industries |\\n| **customer_segment** | Corporate |\\n| **risk_category** | Low |\\n| **internal_rating** | A |\\n| **product_id** | PROD002 |\\n| **product_name** | Term Loan |\\n| **product_type** | Loan |\\n| **pricing_method** | Floating |\\n| **max_discount_allowed_pct** | 0.6 |\\n| **currency** | AED |\\n| **tenor** | 12M |\\n| **requested_amount** | 58,000,000 |\\n| **funding_cost_pct** | 5.55 |\\n| **standard_margin_pct** | 2.1 |\\n| **risk_premium_pct** | 0.1 |\\n| **relationship_discount_pct** | 0.45 |\\n| **recommended_price_pct** | 7.3 |\\n| **final_approved_price_pct** | 7.25 |\\n| **expected_margin_pct** | 1.35 |\\n| **deal_outcome** | Won |\\n| **sales_channel** | API Quote |\\n| **policy_min_margin_pct** | 2.0 |\\n| **policy_min_expected_margin_pct** | 0.75 |\\n| **policy_max_discount_pct** | 0.45 |\\n| **policy_rwa_risk_weight_pct** | 50 |\\n| **price_below_policy_floor** | 0 |\\n| **margin_below_min** | 0 |\\n| **discount_exceeds_policy** | 0 |\\n| **policy_compliant** | 1 |\\n\\n**Key Figures Requested:**\\n* **Recommended Price:** `7.3%`\\n* **Expected Margin:** `1.35%`\\n* **Compliance Status:** **Fully Compliant** (`policy_compliant: 1`). All compliance flags are clear: `price_below_policy_floor: 0`, `margin_below_min: 0`, and `discount_exceeds_policy: 0`.\\n\\n*Source: pricing_recommendation*'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:51:49+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "9cb7492188c8bd799f9c57e49bb8875a", "span_id": "8b66c3f7d16cc9e0", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "7A3DF87F", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call', 'id': 'fc_ffa6c21a-fb9b-4ca6-aae1-fdbf03471bad', 'name': 'query_knowledge_base', 'arguments': '{\"question\":\"What are the model validation requirements in the Model Risk Management (MRM) framework at First Abu Dhabi Bank?\"}'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:51:49+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "9cb7492188c8bd799f9c57e49bb8875a", "span_id": "8b66c3f7d16cc9e0", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "7A3DF87F", "msg": "{'role': 'tool', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call_response', 'id': 'fc_ffa6c21a-fb9b-4ca6-aae1-fdbf03471bad', 'response': 'Based on the **FAB Model'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:51:49+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "9cb7492188c8bd799f9c57e49bb8875a", "span_id": "8b66c3f7d16cc9e0", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "7A3DF87F", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call', 'id': 'fc_7ab42fe2-0079-44b9-b3a3-8994e0a09b12', 'name': 'query_knowledge_base', 'arguments': '{\"question\":\"Provide the complete Model Risk Management (MRM) framework model validation requirements for FAB, including documentation, testing, governance, and sign‑off criteria.\"}'}]}"}
{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:51:49+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "9cb7492188c8bd799f9c57e49bb8875a", "span_id": "8b66c3f7d16cc9e0", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "7A3DF87F", "msg": "{'role': 'tool', 'parts': [{'type': 'tool_call_response', 'id': 'fc_7ab42fe2-0079-44b9-b3a3-8994e0a09b12', 'response': \"Based on the **FAB Model Risk Management Framework (v3.1)** and the **CBUAE Circular No. 2024/BSE/047**, the following outlines FAB's comprehensive Model Risk Management (MRM) framework and specific validation requirements.\\n\\n### 1. Governance and Model Classification\\nThe MRM framework aligns with US Federal Reserve (SR 11-7) and CBUAE regulatory standards. The Framework is governed by the Chief Risk Officer and approved by the Board Risk & Compliance Committee.\\n*   **AI Risk Officer**: Senior management (CRO level or above) must be appointed to oversee regulatory compliance **[CBUAE 2024/BSE/047, Art. 2.1.2]**.\\n*   **Model Inventory**: A centralized, up-to-date inventory must be maintained for all AI/ML systems deployed in material business processes **[CBUAE 2024/BSE/047, Art. 2.2.1]**.\\n*   **Risk Classification**: Models are tiered based on materiality:\\n    *   **Tier 1 (High)**: Direct P&L impact or influence on credit decisions/pricing (e.g., IFRS 9 models, Credit Pricing AI agents). *Requirement: Full independent validation before deployment & annually thereafter.*\\n    *   **Tier 2 (Medium)**: Indirect impact (e.g., behavioral scoring). *Requirement: Targeted validation & biennial reviews.*\\n    *   **Tier 3 (Low)**: Minimal impact. *Requirement: Self-certification.*\\n    *(Source: FAB Model Risk Management Framework v3.1, Section 2)*.\\n\\n### 2. Documentation Requirements: The Model Evidence Pack (MEP)\\nFor every Tier 1 or Tier 2 model, a **Model Evidence Pack (MEP)** must be maintained as the primary audit document **[FAB MRM Framework, Sec. 3]**. Mandatory components include:\\n\\n**Core MEP Components:**\\n*   **Model Overview**: Name, ID, purpose, and deployment status.\\n*   **Design Documentation**: Theoretical basis, mathematical formulation, and assumptions.\\n*   **Data & Performance**: Training data sources, quality assessments, and in-sample/out-of-sample performance metrics.\\n*   **Validation Record**: Findings, weaknesses, and remediation actions.\\n*   **Limitations & F\"}]}"}
