{"ts": "2026-06-26T11:54:26+0530", "level": "INFO", "logger": "agent_framework", "trace_id": "9cb7492188c8bd799f9c57e49bb8875a", "span_id": "8b46da4f1dc83f4e", "parent_span_id": "-", "request_id": "7A3DF87F", "msg": "{'role': 'assistant', 'parts': [{'type': 'text', 'content': '**Pricing Recommendation – CUST002**  \\n_Source: query_structured_data (pricing_recommendation)_\\n\\n| Field                         | Value                           |\\n|-------------------------------|---------------------------------|\\n| deal_id                       | DEAL005                         |\\n| deal_date                     | 2025‑10‑24 00:00:00             |\\n| customer_id                   | CUST002                         |\\n| customer_name                 | Falcon Steel Industries         |\\n| customer_segment              | Corporate                       |\\n| risk_category                 | Low                             |\\n| internal_rating               | A                               |\\n| product_id                    | PROD002                         |\\n| product_name                  | Term Loan                       |\\n| product_type                  | Loan                            |\\n| pricing_method                | Floating                        |\\n| max_discount_allowed_pct      | 0.6\\u202f%                           |\\n| currency                      | AED                             |\\n| tenor                         | 12\\u202fM                            |\\n| requested_amount              | 58,000,000                      |\\n| funding_cost_pct              | 5.55\\u202f%                          |\\n| standard_margin_pct           | 2.1\\u202f%                           |\\n| risk_premium_pct              | 0.1\\u202f%                           |\\n| relationship_discount_pct    | 0.45\\u202f%                          |\\n| **recommended_price_pct**     | **7.3\\u202f%**                       |\\n| final_approved_price_pct      | 7.25\\u202f%                          |\\n| **expected_margin_pct**       | **1.35\\u202f%**                      |\\n| deal_outcome                  | Won                             |\\n| sales_channel                 | API Quote                       |\\n| policy_min_margin_pct         | 2.0\\u202f%                           |\\n| policy_min_expected_margin_pct| 0.75\\u202f%                         |\\n| policy_max_discount_pct       | 0.45\\u202f%                          |\\n| policy_rwa_risk_weight_pct    | 50\\u202f%                            |\\n| price_below_policy_floor      | 0                               |\\n| margin_below_min              | 0                               |\\n| discount_exceeds_policy       | 0                               |\\n| **policy_compliant**          | **1\\u202f(Compliant)**               |\\n\\n**Verdict:** The deal for CUST002 is **fully compliant** with all pricing policies (no floor breach, margin meets minimum, discount within limits). Recommended price is 7.3\\u202f% with an expected margin of 1.35\\u202f%.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Model Validation Requirements – FAB Model Risk Management (MRM) Framework**  \\n_Source: query_knowledge_base (FAB Model Risk Management Framework v3.1 & CBUAE Circular No.\\u202f2024/BSE/047)_\\n\\n> **1. Documentation Requirements**  \\n> FAB requires a comprehensive **Model Evidence Pack (MEP)** for all Tier\\u202f1 (High) and Tier\\u202f2 (Medium) models. This serves as the primary audit document and must include:  \\n> • **Model Overview & Design:** Unique model ID, purpose, theoretical basis, mathematical formulation, assumptions/limitations. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f3.1)*  \\n> • **Data Documentation:** Full data dictionary, data lineage from source to model input, data‑quality assessments, training period details. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f3.1; CBUAE Circular Art\\u202f3.1.2)*  \\n> • **Validation Record:** Independent validation findings, identified weaknesses, management responses, and outstanding remediation actions. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f3.1)*  \\n> • **Performance Metrics:** In‑sample and out‑of‑sample testing results, benchmarking against challenger models, cross‑validation outcomes. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f3.1)*  \\n> • **Human‑Override Record:** Trend analysis of human override rates for the preceding 12\\u202fmonths. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f3.1)*  \\n> • **Centralised AI Model Inventory:** Tracks deployment dates, ownership, validation status, and risk classifications. *(CBUAE Circular Art\\u202f2.2.1)*  \\n\\n> **2. Testing Requirements**  \\n> Testing is tier‑based:  \\n> • **Methodological Testing:** Replication of development methodology, sensitivity analysis, conceptual soundness assessment. *(CBUAE Circular Art\\u202f3.2.2)*  \\n> • **Performance Benchmarking:** Compare against alternative approaches, challenger models, or expert judgment. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f3.1)*  \\n> • **Pricing‑Specific Testing (for credit‑pricing models):**  \\n>   – Verify pricing floor compliance mechanisms. *(CBUAE Circular Art\\u202f3.2.3)*  \\n>   – Evaluate effectiveness of human‑oversight controls. *(CBUAE Circular Art\\u202f3.2.3)*  \\n>   – Stress‑test model behaviour under adverse market conditions. *(CBUAE Circular Art\\u202f3.2.3)*  \\n> • **Data Input Testing:** Confirm that interest‑rate/FTP and risk‑rating inputs are sourced from authorised internal systems without undocumented manual overrides. *(CBUAE Circular Art\\u202f7.1.2)*  \\n\\n> **3. Governance Requirements**  \\n> • **Board & Executive Oversight:** Annual review and approval of the AI Governance Policy by the Board; an **AI Risk Officer** (CRO‑level or higher) oversees implementation. *(CBUAE Circular Art\\u202f2.1.1\\u202f&\\u202f2.1.2)*  \\n> • **Independent Validation Separation:** Validation must be performed by a function organisationally separate from model development. *(CBUAE Circular Art\\u202f3.2.1)*  \\n> • **Human‑Override Monitoring:** Continuous monitoring of human overrides with escalation thresholds defined; overrides must be documented and justified. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f3.1)*  \\n> • **Change Management:** Any model change (parameter, data, algorithm) triggers a re‑validation cycle proportionate to the change’s materiality. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f4.2)*  \\n\\n> **4. Sign‑off Criteria**  \\n> • **Validation Sign‑off:** Independent validator signs off confirming that:  \\n>   – All documentation is complete and accurate.  \\n>   – Testing results meet or exceed predefined performance thresholds (e.g., ≥\\u202f95\\u202f% back‑testing accuracy for Tier\\u202f1 credit models).  \\n>   – No material weaknesses remain unresolved.  \\n>   – Governance approvals (AI Risk Officer, Model Owner, Chief Risk Officer) are obtained. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f5.1)*  \\n> • **Model Deployment Approval:** Requires joint sign‑off from Model Owner, AI Risk Officer, and Head of the Business Line. Deployment is prohibited until all sign‑off boxes are ticked in the Model Evidence Pack. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f5.2)*  \\n> • **Periodic Re‑validation:**  \\n>   – Tier\\u202f1 models: at least annually, or sooner if a material change occurs.  \\n>   – Tier\\u202f2 models: every two years, or upon material change.  \\n>   – Tier\\u202f3 models: self‑certification with biennial review. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f6.1)*  \\n\\n> **5. Reporting & Escalation**  \\n> • **Validation Report:** A formal report is stored in the central repository and submitted to the Model Risk Committee.  \\n> • **Escalation:** Any breach of validation standards or unexplained performance degradation is escalated to the Model Risk Committee within 5\\u202fbusiness days. *(FAB MRM Framework v3.1, Sec\\u202f7.1)*  \\n\\nThese requirements ensure that all FAB models—particularly those influencing pricing and credit decisions—are robust, well‑documented, independently validated, and governed in line with both internal policy and CBUAE regulatory expectations.'}]}"}
